  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What the handoff validates",
      "items": [
        "Brief: task, agent, source snapshot, owned paths, planned checks and stop condition.",
        "Result: current source, declared changes, actual checks, findings and uncertainty.",
        "Codex accepts the exact result; blocked or cancelled work can close explicitly unused."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Independent review and freshness",
      "items": [
        "The reviewer differs from the coordinator and implementation workers; every finding gets an evidence-backed disposition.",
        "Complete worker/check evidence before accepting final review. Source or worker/check changes can stale it.",
        "Refresh only affected evidence, assign a new current review when needed, then refresh final adviser context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Global workflow, proportionate gates",
      "items": [
        "Delegation is optional: direct Codex work skips steps 06–09. Each project supplies its checks; small and unchanged read-only tasks keep their lighter path.",
        "Advisers receive the same permitted evidence. Unavailable coverage is recorded; Codex decides against sources.",
        "New v2 records enforce these gates. V1 records keep their rules; declarations grant no process isolation or extra permission."
      ]
    }
  ],
